<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70658" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νηλεύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Neleus,</i> father of <i><span class="en">
				Nestor
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.683
			</span></i>, al.:—Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νηλήϊος</span></b> , 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">υἱός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.20
				</span></i>
			:—Patron. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νηλεΐδης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου,</span>
			
				Ep.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱο</span>, ὁ, <i><span class="en">
				23.652
			</span></i>; 
				Ep.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νηληϊάδης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εω</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱο</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				8.100
			</span></i>, al.: in fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νηληΐς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ΐδος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.120
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νηλεύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>, ὁ, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νείλεως</span>
			, founder of Miletus, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.94.4
			</span></i> (written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νελ</span>-), <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Dian.</u>
				226
			</span></i>: hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νειλεΐδης</span></b> ,
			and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νειληϊάδης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου,</span>
			
				Ep.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱο</span>, ὁ, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.Aet.
				3.26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νειλεῖον.</span></div>
